  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NIHR Global Health Centre for Multiple Long Term Conditions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Centre aims to:(i) improve care for people living with MLTC in both countries by co-designing, implementing and evaluating a contextually relevant, patient-centred, equity promoting, simple technology leveraged innovative health system interventionand (ii) strengthen national health research systems by capacity building, creating networks of MLTC researchers and key stakeholders, using &#x2018;systems&#x2019; (individual, institutional and environments) thinking.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The NIHR Global Health Centre for Multiple Long Term Conditions is collaborative centre for excellence jointly led by the University of Leicester and Public Health Foundation of India, with two further collaborators in India (HRIDAY, Delhi and AIIMS Jodhpur) and one in Nepal (Kathmandu Medical College), with a remit of conducting high-quality research and building research capacity of the LMIC members in the area of multiple long term conditions.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The target groups are people living with multiple long term conditions in both rural and urban areas in India and Nepal</narrative>
  </description>
